WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.001 --> 00:01.022
(All characters, locations, and events are fictional

3
00:01.047 --> 00:02.022
and for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:02.047 --> 00:02.998
No actions depicted are intended to be encouraged or endorsed.

5
00:03.023 --> 00:03.990
Animals were specially trained and supervised by professionals.

6
00:04.015 --> 00:04.994
Viewer discretion is advised.)

7
00:05.081 --> 00:07.871
Golf teaches us that no day is ever perfect.

8
00:13.136 --> 00:15.855
But every day can still end beautifully.

9
00:15.880 --> 00:18.761
Some holes are pars, while others we may go a little over.

10
00:19.930 --> 00:21.457
But if we make it all the way to the 18th hole

11
00:21.482 --> 00:24.061
with a steady heart and a steadfast spirit,

12
00:26.197 --> 00:27.954
then it's been a good day.

13
00:28.829 --> 00:30.784
And when it comes to relationships,

14
00:30.809 --> 00:33.532
no matter what we go through, all we need is someone to stay

15
00:33.557 --> 00:37.885
and say, "Are you tired? Thank you for today."

16
00:37.910 --> 00:41.062
Because in the end, life isn't a competition to beat anyone.

17
00:41.617 --> 00:44.743
It's about playing a round with someone who makes you feel

18
00:44.768 --> 00:46.999
that no matter how tough the hole,

19
00:47.696 --> 00:49.047
you'll still want to start over,

20
00:49.071 --> 00:51.366
hold hands, and walk into tomorrow together.

21
00:55.573 --> 01:02.408
(Pro Arm - Arthitaya Kunalaphat)

22
01:08.456 --> 01:12.025
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪

23
01:12.668 --> 01:14.313
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

24
01:14.338 --> 01:18.095
♪ It's plain to see ♪

25
01:18.120 --> 01:20.183
♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

26
01:20.252 --> 01:23.688
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

27
01:24.285 --> 01:26.078
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪

28
01:26.103 --> 01:29.940
♪ Everywhere I go, you're by my side ♪

29
01:29.967 --> 01:31.797
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

30
01:31.821 --> 01:34.669
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

31
01:34.694 --> 01:36.574
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

32
01:36.599 --> 01:39.411
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

33
01:39.436 --> 01:42.330
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

34
01:42.355 --> 01:46.155
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

35
01:46.180 --> 01:48.180
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

36
01:48.205 --> 01:50.907
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

37
01:50.932 --> 01:54.438
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

38
01:54.463 --> 01:59.232
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

39
01:59.257 --> 02:01.204
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

40
02:03.037 --> 02:05.263
Today's main agenda is

41
02:05.288 --> 02:09.538
the All Star Women's Golf Tournament.

42
02:09.904 --> 02:11.869
The Golf Course Network is organizing

43
02:11.894 --> 02:13.606
the All Star Women's Golf Tournament.

44
02:13.630 --> 02:17.548
So I was thinking of sending you to represent Goodview.

45
02:17.573 --> 02:19.163
I'd rather not compete.

46
02:19.188 --> 02:20.202
Why not?

47
02:20.227 --> 02:22.085
There are some things I'd rather not explain.

48
02:22.110 --> 02:25.126
What happened that day has stayed with Vee all this time.

49
02:25.169 --> 02:27.281
It was the final day of the tournament.

50
02:27.306 --> 02:29.180
Her father had a heart attack.

51
02:29.205 --> 02:31.205
By the time Vee got to the hospital,

52
02:31.949 --> 02:33.269
it was too late.

53
02:50.522 --> 02:52.068
You want me to compete

54
02:52.855 --> 02:55.133
because you want our course to become famous again, right?

55
02:55.319 --> 02:57.005
You want everything to go perfectly,

56
02:57.030 --> 02:58.861
just like you planned.

57
02:59.036 --> 03:01.210
But my golfing career

58
03:01.586 --> 03:03.532
was never that beautiful.

59
03:04.492 --> 03:07.258
Everything fell apart the day I chose the trophy

60
03:07.809 --> 03:09.243
instead of my father.

61
03:41.519 --> 03:44.249
And now you're asking me to choose again.

62
03:44.749 --> 03:46.852
Between my pain

63
03:47.757 --> 03:49.542
and your success.

64
03:51.487 --> 03:54.316
And you should know what I'll choose.

65
04:19.107 --> 04:20.734
Hello, Pro Vee.

66
04:23.358 --> 04:24.373
Hello.

67
04:25.450 --> 04:27.550
I just finished my lesson with Pro Wan.

68
04:27.827 --> 04:30.415
I've gotten a lot better lately.

69
04:30.440 --> 04:32.071
I'll probably be ready for a round soon.

70
04:32.639 --> 04:37.296
It'd be great if I could play my first round with you, Pro Vee.

71
04:39.650 --> 04:42.692
Are you free, Pro Vee? Want to grab something to eat?

72
04:42.717 --> 04:45.885
I'm sorry, but I already have plans.

73
04:47.723 --> 04:50.161
You really have plans?

74
04:50.186 --> 04:52.808
Or are you turning me down

75
04:53.141 --> 04:54.673
because you're worried about Nana?

76
04:56.216 --> 04:58.558
- Um... - I can tell.

77
04:58.917 --> 05:04.627
Well, you two are way too close for a course owner and a pro.

78
05:04.882 --> 05:08.131
Even the grass on the green can tell.

79
05:12.225 --> 05:13.313
Pro Vee.

80
05:14.687 --> 05:17.219
Can I be honest with you about something?

81
05:20.814 --> 05:24.181
I've been thinking long and hard about whether I should say this,

82
05:24.206 --> 05:26.919
but I'd feel terrible if I didn't tell you.

83
05:28.818 --> 05:30.061
Tell me what?

84
05:31.608 --> 05:32.791
It's about Nana.

85
05:34.264 --> 05:40.769
The truth is, Nana never had serious feelings for you.

86
05:41.910 --> 05:44.321
When she told us

87
05:44.346 --> 05:46.689
about having to manage this course,

88
05:47.498 --> 05:52.648
Wow, you've got quite the list of plans, Miss Nana.

89
05:52.673 --> 05:54.912
Yeah. You think you can handle it?

90
05:54.937 --> 05:56.819
The course is huge.

91
05:56.844 --> 05:58.806
You've got so much to deal with.

92
05:59.178 --> 06:00.808
I've got Nut to help me.

93
06:01.952 --> 06:03.755
Can Nut handle all that on his own?

94
06:03.780 --> 06:04.977
Exactly.

95
06:05.519 --> 06:07.130
Let me tell you,

96
06:07.155 --> 06:09.942
you need to put that irresistible charm of yours to use.

97
06:09.967 --> 06:13.463
Win over the people you think can help you the most.

98
06:14.590 --> 06:15.828
How, Meow?

99
06:17.202 --> 06:20.136
If that person falls for your charm,

100
06:20.743 --> 06:23.782
they'll do anything for you.

101
06:24.364 --> 06:27.557
Not because it's their job or because they're getting paid,

102
06:27.863 --> 06:30.327
but because they genuinely want to help you.

103
06:30.995 --> 06:34.635
Get four or five people like that at the course, and you're set.

104
06:35.295 --> 06:36.350
Really?

105
06:36.703 --> 06:40.250
Just work that charm of yours, you little heiress.

106
06:42.071 --> 06:44.914
Then start with that golf pro you told us about.

107
07:02.179 --> 07:04.918
I never thought Nana would actually do it.

108
07:06.555 --> 07:09.505
I don't want to see you take her seriously all by yourself.

109
07:10.174 --> 07:12.041
You're a good person, Pro Vee.

110
07:12.066 --> 07:14.979
You shouldn't be used as someone's pawn.

111
07:16.382 --> 07:18.792
I don't want to see you get hurt in the end.

112
07:32.834 --> 07:34.151
This pen is great, Belle.

113
07:34.176 --> 07:36.152
I've signed so many papers and my hand doesn't even hurt.

114
07:36.177 --> 07:38.862
And it comes in so many colors. Love it.

115
07:43.778 --> 07:44.996
Thank you.

116
07:46.440 --> 07:47.916
I'm actually pretty excited, Belle.

117
07:50.211 --> 07:52.972
You think it'll turn out well, right?

118
07:53.695 --> 07:54.956
Of course.

119
07:55.346 --> 07:58.661
Everyone's already more than halfway through the preparations.

120
07:58.686 --> 08:01.145
Everyone knows this All Star tournament

121
08:01.170 --> 08:04.729
will be another event that puts our course back on the map.

122
08:04.994 --> 08:07.512
And if Pro Vee wins the championship,

123
08:07.537 --> 08:10.363
we'll get to host an Asian Tour event.

124
08:10.388 --> 08:12.402
That would put us on the map across Asia.

125
08:14.711 --> 08:17.299
Pro Vee still hasn't agreed to represent our course.

126
08:17.793 --> 08:18.816
Oh.

127
08:19.298 --> 08:21.392
But a lot of people are trying to convince her.

128
08:23.449 --> 08:25.563
And if it's not Pro Vee,

129
08:25.588 --> 08:27.271
who would you choose, Miss Nana?

130
08:28.113 --> 08:29.573
I haven't thought that far ahead.

131
08:30.347 --> 08:32.975
Oh, have you talked to Pro Jin?

132
08:33.000 --> 08:35.270
How's she doing over at the Royal Green?

133
08:35.899 --> 08:38.891
Mm, she's doing okay. I heard that lately...

134
08:41.062 --> 08:43.422
Are you busy, Nana? I have a plan to pitch.

135
08:43.447 --> 08:45.520
I want the pro who's competing in the All Star

136
08:45.545 --> 08:47.856
to help test out our golf game.

137
08:48.158 --> 08:49.864
It could help promote it, too.

138
08:49.896 --> 08:51.607
Do you have 20 minutes to hear me out?

139
08:51.632 --> 08:52.663
Sure, Gus.

140
08:53.393 --> 08:55.004
I'll leave you two to it, then.

141
08:57.962 --> 08:59.481
Okay, let's hear it.

142
08:59.829 --> 09:02.530
It's about the latest technology being used in golf,

143
09:02.555 --> 09:04.784
like distance-measuring tech.

144
09:12.009 --> 09:13.017
Pro Vee.

145
09:14.747 --> 09:16.239
Can I talk to you for a minute?

146
09:17.405 --> 09:20.136
Is it about competing in the All Star?

147
09:20.810 --> 09:21.896
Yes.

148
09:21.929 --> 09:23.958
Nana said you haven't agreed yet,

149
09:24.533 --> 09:25.605
so I thought...

150
09:25.630 --> 09:27.949
You thought it'd be good for the course

151
09:27.974 --> 09:30.663
and good for me, right?

152
09:35.506 --> 09:38.616
But I respect whatever decision you make.

153
09:40.580 --> 09:43.375
Pro Vee, you have a visitor.

154
09:43.670 --> 09:47.156
Okay. I'll excuse myself for now.

155
09:59.747 --> 10:02.544
What's wrong? Why did you come all the way to the course?

156
10:06.387 --> 10:08.648
I made your favorite chicken soup.

157
10:08.673 --> 10:10.172
I brought some for Nana, too.

158
10:11.139 --> 10:14.509
Someone asked you to come talk to me about the All Star?

159
10:18.929 --> 10:20.414
I understand you, Vee.

160
10:21.112 --> 10:23.335
But it happened a long time ago.

161
10:24.418 --> 10:28.469
But to me, Mom, it feels like it just happened yesterday.

162
10:29.195 --> 10:30.226
Vee...

163
10:31.823 --> 10:34.967
How long are you going to stay stuck in that moment?

164
10:35.518 --> 10:38.537
And if I compete this time,

165
10:39.492 --> 10:41.492
what will I have to lose again, Mom?

166
10:41.974 --> 10:43.941
But just because you don't compete

167
10:44.314 --> 10:47.711
doesn't mean you won't lose anything, sweetheart.

168
10:48.952 --> 10:50.273
What do you mean?

169
10:52.495 --> 10:55.474
You're going to lose the opportunities life has to offer.

170
10:55.895 --> 10:59.488
What happened that day made you close yourself off

171
10:59.513 --> 11:01.513
from going any further.

172
11:01.999 --> 11:03.556
Think about it, sweetheart.

173
11:05.167 --> 11:06.587
Deep down,

174
11:07.614 --> 11:11.035
what is your ultimate goal on your journey in golf?

175
11:13.934 --> 11:16.236
And what is your goal in life?

176
11:17.124 --> 11:19.124
What you're doing right now,

177
11:19.590 --> 11:21.533
when will it get you there?

178
11:22.217 --> 11:23.836
And most importantly,

179
11:25.490 --> 11:27.493
what is your heart telling you now?

180
11:28.398 --> 11:30.080
What is it telling you to do?

181
11:31.185 --> 11:32.768
And who are you doing it for?

182
11:57.323 --> 11:59.090
- Chef Queen. - Yes?

183
11:59.115 --> 12:01.115
Have you seen Pro Vee today?

184
12:01.483 --> 12:04.737
Oh, Pro Vee should be teaching a lesson today.

185
12:07.850 --> 12:13.238
Ooh, why does the mood feel so gloomy today?

186
12:13.474 --> 12:14.679
Did you two have a fight?

187
12:15.488 --> 12:17.193
Like tongue and teeth,

188
12:17.218 --> 12:19.637
people living together are bound to clash.

189
12:19.903 --> 12:22.853
When you're in love. Oh, take it easy, talk it out.

190
12:22.878 --> 12:24.602
A word or two and you'll make up.

191
12:24.627 --> 12:25.753
Oh!

192
12:26.283 --> 12:28.469
Did I just say "in love"?

193
12:28.494 --> 12:30.980
Wait, did I say that right?

194
12:31.005 --> 12:33.094
How did that just slip out?

195
12:33.119 --> 12:35.119
Was that even right?

196
12:35.144 --> 12:38.263
You know, love is like a raging bull.

197
12:38.288 --> 12:41.466
When it gets late at night... Hey, Miss!

198
12:43.529 --> 12:45.918
You act like I'm invisible!

199
12:46.323 --> 12:49.086
I'm all alone. I'm lonely.

200
12:49.111 --> 12:51.423
You come around, then you disappear.

201
12:51.448 --> 12:53.448
And then there's no one here at all.

202
12:53.623 --> 12:56.482
Who brought me flowers? Thank you!

203
13:19.263 --> 13:20.398
Pro Vee.

204
13:22.274 --> 13:24.123
There's something I want to talk to you about.

205
13:24.497 --> 13:26.340
- Well... - I've decided.

206
13:26.928 --> 13:29.872
I'll represent our course in the All Star tournament.

207
13:33.815 --> 13:35.032
What do you mean?

208
13:36.405 --> 13:38.525
I'm going to compete in the All Star.

209
13:38.550 --> 13:41.872
But there's something I want to ask you.

210
13:42.811 --> 13:44.033
What is it?

211
13:44.610 --> 13:48.821
Fahsai told me that the reason you've been so nice to me

212
13:48.846 --> 13:50.506
was because you were trying to charm me,

213
13:50.720 --> 13:52.707
so you could use me.

214
13:52.732 --> 13:55.024
But I don't believe that.

215
13:55.049 --> 13:57.667
I just want to hear you say that's not true.

216
13:57.692 --> 13:59.914
I would never do something like that.

217
14:00.229 --> 14:02.938
You know how real what we have is.

218
14:03.895 --> 14:07.221
And about wanting you to compete again,

219
14:08.309 --> 14:10.494
I understand you were only trying to help.

220
14:10.722 --> 14:14.403
And I want to thank you for making me see things differently.

221
14:16.807 --> 14:19.141
I want to apologize to you, too.

222
14:19.737 --> 14:22.285
I was a little too harsh that day.

223
14:23.731 --> 14:25.227
A little?

224
14:25.252 --> 14:27.647
But it did make me realize some things.

225
14:28.122 --> 14:31.813
Let's just say everything happens for a reason.

226
14:31.838 --> 14:33.170
Have you heard that before?

227
14:35.594 --> 14:39.962
Vee, I don't want you to think that by competing again,

228
14:40.283 --> 14:41.765
you're doing it for the course,

229
14:41.789 --> 14:43.929
for me, or for anyone else.

230
14:44.960 --> 14:46.960
You're doing it for yourself.

231
14:49.406 --> 14:50.969
But that's not entirely true.

232
14:51.628 --> 14:53.502
Because if it weren't for you,

233
14:53.527 --> 14:55.700
I wouldn't have thought about competing again.

234
14:56.437 --> 14:58.190
As for this competition,

235
14:58.215 --> 15:01.079
the first thing I want to do is make you happy.

236
15:02.157 --> 15:05.910
As for me, I'll just consider that a little bonus.

237
15:05.935 --> 15:09.503
I think it's a good thing that this bonus is an opportunity.

238
15:10.027 --> 15:13.261
An opportunity to reconnect with my feelings,

239
15:13.286 --> 15:15.324
to reconnect with my own heart.

240
15:20.742 --> 15:23.398
But what if the victory you're about to win

241
15:24.407 --> 15:26.407
ends up pulling us apart?

242
15:27.554 --> 15:28.723
How would it?

243
15:31.621 --> 15:33.852
If everything goes perfectly,

244
15:34.343 --> 15:35.777
you win the championship,

245
15:36.650 --> 15:39.359
and our course gets to host the Asian Tour,

246
15:39.750 --> 15:41.411
everything will fall into place.

247
15:42.642 --> 15:44.721
The course will regain its reputation,

248
15:45.139 --> 15:46.892
and turn a profit again.

249
15:48.805 --> 15:50.805
And I'll go back to France.

250
15:52.535 --> 15:54.853
That's all in the future.

251
15:54.892 --> 15:58.005
But right now, you're still here with me.

252
16:03.470 --> 16:05.682
Let me do this for you first.

253
16:06.102 --> 16:08.904
And I'll give it everything I've got.

254
16:11.214 --> 16:12.897
Thank you, Vee.

255
16:14.350 --> 16:17.404
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

256
16:17.429 --> 16:20.030
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

257
16:20.055 --> 16:24.149
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

258
16:24.174 --> 16:29.660
♪ Even when the storm rolls in or tears fill your eyes ♪

259
16:30.276 --> 16:34.321
♪ Turn around, you'll find me right by your side ♪

260
16:34.347 --> 16:37.995
♪ Even when the whole world turns unkind ♪

261
16:38.020 --> 16:40.418
♪ You won't be left behind ♪

262
16:40.443 --> 16:45.342
♪ Cause I'll always be right here by your side ♪

263
17:21.792 --> 17:23.755
It's good to have a pro like her back.

264
17:23.780 --> 17:26.175
I was a little disappointed when she left.

265
17:27.083 --> 17:28.974
She's a talented pro.

266
17:30.474 --> 17:31.723
What's her name again?

267
17:32.791 --> 17:33.869
Pro Jin.

268
17:35.076 --> 17:38.187
Jinny, who's fueled by resentment.

269
17:39.733 --> 17:43.543
And that resentment will bring our course the victory.

270
17:44.848 --> 17:47.089
Good. That's clever.

271
17:48.298 --> 17:51.665
Turn that anger and resentment into a weapon.

272
17:52.570 --> 17:54.851
Someone who competes with that kind of emotion

273
17:54.876 --> 17:56.518
won't give up easily.

274
17:57.149 --> 17:58.775
See? Now you understand, Ms. Yupadee.

275
17:59.350 --> 18:01.716
I've got everything planned out.

276
18:02.596 --> 18:05.742
Enough talk. It's just a plan.

277
18:06.362 --> 18:08.048
I'm waiting to see results.

278
18:11.600 --> 18:12.660
You have my word.

279
18:13.112 --> 18:15.152
I've got plenty of backup plans, too.

280
18:41.547 --> 18:44.041
Hiding over there? You think I can't see you?

281
18:48.507 --> 18:51.200
I didn't want to distract you.

282
18:52.365 --> 18:53.510
You wouldn't distract me.

283
18:54.223 --> 18:57.078
In fact, you make me want to practice even harder.

284
18:58.039 --> 19:01.471
Then here. Some motivation you can actually eat.

285
19:01.496 --> 19:04.562
Hmm, but...

286
19:04.587 --> 19:08.081
Looks like you'll have to feed me yourself.

287
19:10.061 --> 19:11.179
Sure.

288
19:11.434 --> 19:13.761
Here... nom!

289
19:19.249 --> 19:20.627
Mmm.

290
19:24.930 --> 19:26.484
Sweeter than I expected.

291
19:26.509 --> 19:27.667
The dessert?

292
19:27.692 --> 19:29.135
The one feeding me.

293
19:29.160 --> 19:31.160
Sweet and fragrant.

294
19:32.023 --> 19:33.648
Can I have another kiss?

295
19:33.673 --> 19:35.889
It'll give me the motivation to keep practicing.

296
19:36.508 --> 19:38.537
A golfer this good at sweet-talking...

297
19:38.562 --> 19:39.998
Besides winning the championship,

298
19:40.023 --> 19:42.824
you're going to win all four chambers of my heart, too.

299
19:44.421 --> 19:45.456
Hmm?

300
19:47.885 --> 19:48.976
Want another bite?

301
19:50.971 --> 19:52.170
Hmm.

302
19:54.156 --> 19:56.538
Mmm, this tastes even better.

303
19:57.302 --> 20:00.493
I'll feed you. Nom!

304
20:01.274 --> 20:02.466
Want to share?

305
20:06.491 --> 20:11.020
Mmm-hmm. It's so sweet.

306
20:11.315 --> 20:14.509
Even tastier, tastier, tastier!

307
20:15.688 --> 20:16.711
Here.

308
20:17.384 --> 20:19.124
I haven't even finished chewing.

309
20:30.277 --> 20:31.648
You're so good.

310
20:31.673 --> 20:35.143
♪ Everyone can tell by the way you stare ♪ You got this!

311
20:35.875 --> 20:37.741
♪ Sneaking little looks when I'm unaware ♪

312
20:37.766 --> 20:43.493
♪ It's plain to see ♪ ♪ I know exactly what you think of me ♪

313
20:43.518 --> 20:46.878
♪ First to watch my stories every time ♪

314
20:47.525 --> 20:49.158
♪ You remember every fave of mine ♪ Thank you.

315
20:49.191 --> 20:51.191
- Thank you. - Thank you.

316
20:52.913 --> 20:54.989
♪ Don't tell me there's nothing on your mind ♪

317
20:55.014 --> 20:57.873
♪ So when are you gonna say the words? ♪

318
20:57.898 --> 20:59.867
♪ Don't keep me waiting till it hurts ♪

319
20:59.892 --> 21:02.680
♪ The way you act, I know you're into me ♪

320
21:02.705 --> 21:05.541
♪ That racing heart gives you away so easily ♪

321
21:05.566 --> 21:09.359
♪ But I'll play clueless, just wait and see ♪

322
21:09.384 --> 21:11.333
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

323
21:11.341 --> 21:14.266
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

324
21:14.291 --> 21:17.659
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

325
21:17.684 --> 21:22.421
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

326
21:22.446 --> 21:24.552
♪ Or should I be the one to call your bluff? ♪

327
21:25.911 --> 21:27.019
Here, have some water.

328
21:27.043 --> 21:29.718
♪ Call it just a little crush♪ But you don't hide it well enough♪

329
21:29.743 --> 21:32.642
♪ Say that there's nothing on your mind But no one's buying that little lie ♪

330
21:32.667 --> 21:33.900
You got this!

331
21:33.925 --> 21:35.408
- Thanks. - Fighting!

332
21:38.045 --> 21:39.108
Great job.

333
21:42.602 --> 21:44.643
Hey, isn't that my water?

334
21:45.048 --> 21:46.303
It's hot and I'm thirsty, too.

335
21:48.025 --> 21:49.408
Thanks.

336
21:52.955 --> 21:54.141
(Belle - Jinny)

337
21:54.803 --> 21:57.914
♪ Giving me signs, so why still wait? ♪

338
21:57.939 --> 22:01.362
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

339
22:01.387 --> 22:05.199
♪ How long will you keep playing so tough? ♪

340
22:05.224 --> 22:08.364
Hello. This event is full of talented pros.

341
22:08.389 --> 22:10.541
- He'll be here. We'll talk then. - Hello. Please, come.

342
22:13.715 --> 22:15.812
- Oh, Uncle. Hello. - Oh, Nana.

343
22:15.837 --> 22:16.961
Hello, sweetheart.

344
22:16.986 --> 22:18.985
Wow, what a lucky day.

345
22:19.010 --> 22:21.226
I get to see the talented CEO of this place.

346
22:21.251 --> 22:23.824
I've known you since you were little,

347
22:23.849 --> 22:25.849
running around here all the time.

348
22:26.234 --> 22:27.887
Here you go. Please, come in.

349
22:27.912 --> 22:30.865
I'm actually organizing a golf tournament here.

350
22:31.237 --> 22:34.512
Oh, wow. What a shame.

351
22:34.537 --> 22:36.862
It's the same day as my eye surgery.

352
22:36.887 --> 22:39.214
- Maybe next time. - Sure.

353
22:39.239 --> 22:43.115
Oh, by the way, your father has started his chemo, right?

354
22:45.003 --> 22:46.407
- Chemo? - Mm-hmm.

355
23:00.753 --> 23:02.523
Oh, August, my boy.

356
23:04.814 --> 23:08.356
Looks like the CEO called you in for an emergency meeting, too?

357
23:23.255 --> 23:26.751
What's wrong? Why do you two look so serious?

358
23:26.751 --> 23:28.449
What's going on, kids?

359
23:29.081 --> 23:30.556
Come on, tell me.

360
23:30.581 --> 23:32.984
Why did you call me here so urgently?

361
23:51.223 --> 23:52.262
What's wrong, kids?

362
23:54.519 --> 23:55.940
- Dad. - Hmm?

363
23:57.642 --> 24:00.126
Is there something you need to tell us?

364
24:03.527 --> 24:05.585
Why are you asking me such strange questions?

365
24:05.610 --> 24:07.347
What do you want me to say?

366
24:10.646 --> 24:13.782
Something the two of us should know about.

367
24:18.820 --> 24:23.023
Oh, you mean the land I bought in Khao Yai?

368
24:23.048 --> 24:25.384
- Or the mine... - Your cancer.

369
24:38.777 --> 24:40.088
Who told you?

370
24:46.119 --> 24:47.713
Why didn't you tell us, Dad?

371
24:50.918 --> 24:53.954
I was afraid you'd both end up like this.

372
24:55.454 --> 24:56.890
But don't worry, sweetheart.

373
24:57.654 --> 25:00.166
I'm about to start my chemo treatment.

374
25:04.015 --> 25:05.077
When?

375
25:06.339 --> 25:07.935
Soon.

376
25:16.062 --> 25:17.674
I love you, Dad.

377
25:21.575 --> 25:23.220
I love you, too, Dad.

378
25:26.779 --> 25:28.226
I love you both, too.

379
25:32.389 --> 25:33.755
I promise.

380
25:35.118 --> 25:39.310
I'll get the best treatment they have to offer.

381
25:46.798 --> 25:49.115
It's okay, sweetheart. Don't cry.

382
25:50.522 --> 25:53.254
Look at your old man. I'm still strong and healthy.

383
25:53.279 --> 25:54.994
I look this healthy,

384
25:55.019 --> 25:58.624
no one would ever know I had cancer if I didn't tell them.

385
25:59.095 --> 26:00.230
Right?

386
26:04.362 --> 26:05.378
It's okay, sweetheart.

387
26:14.830 --> 26:16.540
- Here you go. - Thank you.

388
26:21.315 --> 26:23.255
Aren't you worried they'll tamper with your drink?

389
26:25.060 --> 26:26.791
Is that really all you can think of?

390
26:44.347 --> 26:46.231
Thank you all so much.

391
26:46.256 --> 26:48.274
I know how hard everyone's been working

392
26:48.299 --> 26:49.958
to make this event the best it can be.

393
26:49.982 --> 26:51.133
And it has to be.

394
26:51.713 --> 26:53.244
We're not just aiming for the All Star.

395
26:53.269 --> 26:55.218
We're aiming for the Asian Tour.

396
26:55.337 --> 26:57.526
Does anyone have anything to add today?

397
26:59.803 --> 27:00.820
Anyone?

398
27:01.940 --> 27:03.600
Thank you all for today.

399
27:03.838 --> 27:05.243
Wait, Miss!

400
27:05.268 --> 27:07.325
Shouldn't we have a little "Vive la vie"?

401
27:08.120 --> 27:09.224
Vive la vie!

402
27:09.249 --> 27:11.933
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

403
27:23.819 --> 27:25.972
An army marches on its stomach!

404
27:25.997 --> 27:27.997
Eat up, everyone, then let's get back to work.

405
27:28.022 --> 27:29.086
Go ahead and hand them out.

406
27:29.269 --> 27:32.223
- Wow! - Wow!

407
27:33.386 --> 27:35.148
That looks delicious.

408
27:35.173 --> 27:36.999
- Chef, slacking off today? - Thanks.

409
28:08.710 --> 28:10.321
De-li-ciousss!

410
28:15.860 --> 28:17.812
All right, let's go. We should split up.

411
28:17.837 --> 28:20.083
Ooh, I've got a lot to take care of over there.

412
28:27.299 --> 28:30.817
Oh, I'm thinking of going home tonight.

413
28:30.842 --> 28:32.118
To see your mom?

414
28:33.239 --> 28:36.237
Then give my regards to your mom.

415
28:36.262 --> 28:38.262
Is she coming to the All Star event?

416
28:38.287 --> 28:42.027
Definitely. I hear she's already picked out her outfit.

417
28:42.052 --> 28:45.626
Good. You'll have enough support to fill the whole course.

418
28:45.658 --> 28:47.941
Are you staying at your mom's tonight?

419
28:47.966 --> 28:51.680
Hmm, I'm not sure yet. I'll see how things go first.

420
28:51.705 --> 28:54.320
Then I'll eat dinner here tonight instead of waiting for you.

421
28:55.289 --> 28:57.582
I'll let you know later whether I'm staying or not.

422
28:57.607 --> 28:58.656
Okay.

423
29:13.285 --> 29:15.134
You've seen what Pro Jin can do, right?

424
29:15.159 --> 29:15.943
Mm-hmm.

425
29:17.153 --> 29:18.732
I picked the right person, didn't I?

426
29:20.039 --> 29:21.795
With her in this kind of form,

427
29:21.820 --> 29:24.168
she should have no trouble beating the competition.

428
29:24.564 --> 29:25.580
For me,

429
29:26.395 --> 29:27.949
it's not enough to put up a fight.

430
29:27.974 --> 29:29.409
We have to win.

431
29:31.594 --> 29:34.599
If we get to host the Asian Tour,

432
29:35.433 --> 29:36.597
just think about

433
29:36.622 --> 29:40.788
how many more people will see what our course is capable of.

434
29:40.813 --> 29:42.339
That's my goal.

435
29:45.723 --> 29:46.764
Yes, ma'am.

436
29:47.439 --> 29:49.764
The only pro who can really match Pro Jin

437
29:50.106 --> 29:52.586
is probably Pro Vee from Goodview.

438
29:52.650 --> 29:54.022
Don't get complacent.

439
29:54.615 --> 29:56.569
It wouldn't hurt to have a backup plan.

440
29:57.531 --> 29:58.587
Yes, ma'am.

441
29:59.024 --> 30:01.650
I'm pretty good at playing dirty.

442
30:06.526 --> 30:09.334
- Have a seat, Pro Jin. - Thank you.

443
30:15.926 --> 30:19.718
I want you to bring home the All Star championship.

444
30:19.743 --> 30:21.276
By any means necessary.

445
30:21.301 --> 30:24.303
Of course. We have to win this match.

446
30:24.655 --> 30:27.893
Good. I like that attitude.

447
30:30.046 --> 30:33.915
Oh, and I'd like to ask you to...

448
30:33.940 --> 30:36.110
stay away from the people at Goodview.

449
30:36.579 --> 30:38.025
What does that have to do with anything?

450
30:38.398 --> 30:41.921
They might send that Belle to snoop around our course.

451
30:43.509 --> 30:46.912
People on the other side will never truly be on our side.

452
30:47.999 --> 30:49.629
The closer we get to them,

453
30:50.670 --> 30:51.902
the greater the risk.

454
30:53.061 --> 30:55.394
People who see their rivals as enemies

455
30:55.743 --> 30:57.798
often miss the opportunities right in front of them.

456
30:57.823 --> 31:01.435
Because sometimes, getting close gives us a chance

457
31:01.460 --> 31:03.264
to see what they're hiding.

458
31:04.286 --> 31:05.691
Just like this time.

459
31:06.154 --> 31:08.674
I let her compete for Goodview

460
31:09.070 --> 31:10.113
because normally,

461
31:10.138 --> 31:13.677
we'd never get to see every corner of their course.

462
31:13.701 --> 31:15.185
But this competition

463
31:15.210 --> 31:19.858
will give us a chance to see every corner of their operation.

464
31:20.186 --> 31:23.290
Work with me. Don't think so narrowly.

465
31:23.315 --> 31:24.936
Don't disappoint me.

466
31:26.717 --> 31:30.663
People only remember first place. No one remembers second.

467
31:58.407 --> 32:00.280
(Eat it while it's still hot.)

468
32:31.551 --> 32:34.632
Go ahead and season it to your liking. Okay?

469
32:37.749 --> 32:40.505
Oh, Pro Jin! What brings you here?

470
32:41.204 --> 32:42.362
What a coincidence.

471
32:45.776 --> 32:46.871
Coincidence?

472
32:46.896 --> 32:49.554
Oops. Belle must've tagged the wrong person.

473
32:50.866 --> 32:54.782
Well, since I'm already here, mind if I join you?

474
32:55.465 --> 32:56.543
Please.

475
33:01.374 --> 33:02.469
Have you ordered yet?

476
33:02.494 --> 33:05.136
Not yet. What would you like, Pro Jin?

477
33:05.161 --> 33:06.335
The usual.

478
33:07.066 --> 33:08.092
- Uncle. - Yes?

479
33:08.117 --> 33:09.719
Two dry chicken noodle soups, please.

480
33:09.744 --> 33:10.893
And two bowls of broth, please.

481
33:10.918 --> 33:13.504
Oh, the usual. Coming right up.

482
33:13.599 --> 33:15.218
Are you ready for the competition?

483
33:15.805 --> 33:19.364
Very. This time, I'm going to beat Pro Vee.

484
33:19.389 --> 33:21.264
I want to cheer you on, too.

485
33:21.962 --> 33:23.645
But if you win,

486
33:23.670 --> 33:27.134
that means Goodview won't get the right to host the Asian Tour.

487
33:27.663 --> 33:30.508
But if I cheer for Pro Vee and Goodview,

488
33:30.533 --> 33:32.191
that means you have to lose.

489
33:32.962 --> 33:35.027
And I don't want that either.

490
33:35.547 --> 33:38.197
Even if our courses are rivals,

491
33:38.222 --> 33:39.890
you and I aren't.

492
33:39.915 --> 33:41.915
If you cheer for me that openly,

493
33:42.217 --> 33:43.997
you might need to find a new job.

494
33:45.627 --> 33:48.905
Then I'll just choose to believe

495
33:48.930 --> 33:51.726
that whenever I look over and see you by the sidelines,

496
33:52.117 --> 33:54.117
you're cheering me on in your heart.

497
34:00.264 --> 34:03.620
Here you go. Two noodles.

498
34:03.773 --> 34:09.076
And two bowls of broth, just like usual.

499
34:10.033 --> 34:12.867
Oh, and this...

500
34:17.615 --> 34:18.931
We didn't order this.

501
34:18.956 --> 34:20.844
A pair of shumai. On the house.

502
34:20.869 --> 34:22.553
To make you two a pair sooner.

503
34:39.067 --> 34:40.358
Is this too big?

504
35:16.768 --> 35:17.898
Nana.

505
35:18.789 --> 35:20.131
Vee...

506
35:20.570 --> 35:23.848
What's wrong? Why are you covered in a rash?

507
35:23.873 --> 35:25.516
The soup you brought me...

508
35:25.541 --> 35:27.599
Did it have shrimp in it?

509
35:28.821 --> 35:29.980
What soup?

510
35:30.005 --> 35:32.476
The soup you left outside my house.

511
35:40.284 --> 35:42.996
Nana. Nana!

512
35:43.631 --> 35:44.678
Nana!

513
35:49.963 --> 35:52.788
You're okay now. I've already given you an injection.

514
35:52.813 --> 35:54.177
You probably only ate a little.

515
35:54.771 --> 35:56.428
Just two or three bites.

516
35:57.294 --> 36:00.246
You should stay overnight so we can monitor you.

517
36:00.681 --> 36:03.823
If there are no further symptoms, you can go home tomorrow.

518
36:04.958 --> 36:07.257
Be careful about what you eat from now on.

519
36:07.282 --> 36:10.457
And when you have time, come back for an allergy test.

520
36:10.769 --> 36:12.135
You might be allergic to something else, too.

521
36:13.978 --> 36:15.708
- Okay. - All right.

522
36:17.067 --> 36:18.640
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

523
36:49.745 --> 36:50.954
Are you coming inside?

524
36:52.384 --> 36:53.670
Probably not a good idea.

525
36:54.726 --> 36:58.190
Someone from a rival course coming into my house this late...

526
36:59.575 --> 37:00.654
You're right.

527
37:02.330 --> 37:03.745
Thank you.

528
37:03.770 --> 37:06.229
For what?

529
37:07.967 --> 37:13.332
For the food you sent, the messages,

530
37:13.797 --> 37:15.955
and the support.

531
37:26.206 --> 37:28.359
I wonder what will happen to us.

532
37:29.136 --> 37:30.898
What do you want to happen?

533
37:35.106 --> 37:36.272
I don't know.

534
37:37.026 --> 37:40.164
Why don't we figure that out after the All Star?

535
37:40.734 --> 37:43.629
Right now, we should focus on the competition

536
37:43.654 --> 37:45.169
you've been waiting for.

537
37:47.269 --> 37:48.474
If I win...

538
37:49.492 --> 37:51.143
what happens after that?

539
37:52.483 --> 37:53.870
And if I lose...

540
37:55.570 --> 37:57.705
Let's leave that for the future.

541
37:58.968 --> 38:03.631
For now, let this be your answer.

542
39:48.456 --> 39:49.841
Thank you, Vee.

543
39:50.906 --> 39:54.132
I had someone check the CCTV footage.

544
39:54.157 --> 39:56.464
The person who left the soup for you

545
39:56.489 --> 40:00.240
was wearing a helmet and dressed like an ordinary delivery driver,

546
40:00.265 --> 40:02.222
so they got in easily.

547
40:02.247 --> 40:03.937
We couldn't see their face,

548
40:03.977 --> 40:05.683
and we couldn't see the license plate either.

549
40:07.305 --> 40:09.767
Could they have delivered it to the wrong house?

550
40:10.918 --> 40:13.191
I wish I could believe that, too.

551
40:13.216 --> 40:15.296
That it was just a delivery mix-up,

552
40:15.321 --> 40:17.321
and it just happened to contain shrimp.

553
40:18.078 --> 40:19.355
From now on,

554
40:19.380 --> 40:22.058
you need to be much more careful. Understand?

555
40:23.185 --> 40:25.185
Don't worry about me, Vee.

556
40:25.210 --> 40:26.786
I'll be fine.

557
40:26.811 --> 40:28.550
The competition is almost here.

558
40:28.575 --> 40:30.828
I don't want you to lose focus.

559
40:30.853 --> 40:32.958
I don't want to become a burden to you.

560
40:35.359 --> 40:38.153
You've never been a burden to me.

561
40:38.634 --> 40:42.562
You're the reason I have to win.

562
40:45.147 --> 40:48.649
How are you feeling now? Any better?

563
40:49.030 --> 40:51.482
I felt better the moment I saw you.

564
40:51.527 --> 40:54.375
I always feel safe when you're with me.

565
40:57.792 --> 41:01.623
Oh, you're really good at sweet-talking me.

566
41:02.043 --> 41:05.637
Is this part of your plan to make me fall for you?

567
41:06.757 --> 41:07.821
Oh, come on, Vee...

568
41:08.606 --> 41:10.276
I'm just teasing you.

569
41:10.301 --> 41:13.811
I already know that someone this cute,

570
41:13.836 --> 41:19.370
with this face, this smile, and these eyes...

571
41:19.847 --> 41:22.778
doesn't have to charm me. I'm already head over heels.

572
41:25.687 --> 41:28.136
Come on. You should get some sleep.

573
41:29.446 --> 41:30.541
Get some proper rest.

574
41:32.066 --> 41:34.462
So you'll wake up feeling refreshed tomorrow.

575
41:34.629 --> 41:35.724
Now close your eyes.

576
41:36.666 --> 41:38.653
Tell me a bedtime story.

577
41:38.812 --> 41:40.812
Hmm? A bedtime story?

578
41:41.204 --> 41:43.442
Your mom told me that when we were little,

579
41:43.467 --> 41:45.270
whenever I stayed over at your house,

580
41:45.295 --> 41:47.670
you'd tell me stories until I fell asleep.

581
41:47.695 --> 41:50.877
Wow. Now that you know you can get your way with me,

582
41:50.902 --> 41:52.663
you're really going for it.

583
41:53.440 --> 41:54.669
Rub my hand too, please?

584
41:57.984 --> 42:01.065
Hmm. What story would you like to hear?

585
42:01.398 --> 42:02.525
Anything.

586
42:05.463 --> 42:10.251
Once upon a time, long, long ago,

587
42:10.276 --> 42:12.737
there lived two princesses.

588
42:12.762 --> 42:14.849
A wicked wizard tricked them

589
42:14.874 --> 42:16.574
into venturing deep into the forest,

590
42:16.598 --> 42:18.805
then locked them away in a little cottage.

591
42:28.091 --> 42:31.256
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

592
42:31.281 --> 42:33.717
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

593
42:33.742 --> 42:39.350
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

594
42:39.375 --> 42:42.410
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

595
42:42.435 --> 42:46.707
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

596
42:48.574 --> 42:51.666
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

597
42:51.691 --> 42:54.350
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

598
42:54.375 --> 43:00.014
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

599
43:00.039 --> 43:03.169
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

600
43:03.194 --> 43:05.704
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

601
43:05.729 --> 43:09.319
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

602
43:16.071 --> 43:17.222
Have a seat.

603
43:22.114 --> 43:23.836
I called you here

604
43:23.861 --> 43:25.987
because I want everything to go according to plan.

605
43:27.463 --> 43:28.560
What plan?

606
43:29.959 --> 43:32.070
The plan to make sure you win the championship tomorrow.

607
43:34.126 --> 43:35.618
I don't like leaving things to chance.

608
43:36.332 --> 43:39.918
I want to know for certain, before you even compete,

609
43:39.943 --> 43:41.344
that you're going to win.

610
43:44.052 --> 43:47.564
This is a ball drop device. Just strap it to your ankle.

611
43:47.589 --> 43:50.292
If your ball gets stuck in an unplayable hazard,

612
43:51.412 --> 43:52.556
just tap it lightly,

613
43:52.581 --> 43:53.796
and a new ball will drop out.

614
43:55.068 --> 43:57.999
And this is a rangefinder I modified myself.

615
43:58.024 --> 44:00.944
You can use its slope mode without anyone noticing.

616
44:01.774 --> 44:03.791
But slope mode is against the rules.

617
44:04.711 --> 44:05.862
So is the ball drop device.

618
44:07.418 --> 44:09.493
But we're not talking about right or wrong here.

619
44:10.855 --> 44:12.425
We're talking about winning.

620
44:14.907 --> 44:18.170
So The Royal Green doesn't trust my ability to win on my own.

621
44:19.273 --> 44:20.622
Like I said,

622
44:21.433 --> 44:22.715
I don't like leaving things to chance.

623
44:24.009 --> 44:25.509
I only like to win.

624
44:28.118 --> 44:31.183
I've already gone over everything with your caddie.

625
44:31.972 --> 44:33.751
Don't forget to wear long pants tomorrow.

626
44:34.274 --> 44:35.801
That way, you can hide the device.

627
44:35.865 --> 44:38.565
As for the camera, I'll give it to your caddie.

628
44:39.265 --> 44:40.273
That's the plan.

629
44:56.839 --> 44:59.112
Tomorrow is a big day for our course.

630
44:59.137 --> 45:03.138
I want to thank everyone for giving it your all.

631
45:03.163 --> 45:06.839
The course was once so quiet, but now it's come back to life.

632
45:09.003 --> 45:12.155
Tomorrow will be the first step in proving that

633
45:12.180 --> 45:15.635
our course can rise to the top of the golf industry once again.

634
45:18.774 --> 45:20.340
As for the competition,

635
45:20.365 --> 45:22.618
we're putting our hopes in you, Pro Vee.

636
45:22.987 --> 45:24.947
The road to hosting the Asian Tour

637
45:24.987 --> 45:26.093
is now in your hands.

638
45:26.117 --> 45:28.250
Bring home the win for our course.

639
45:32.566 --> 45:33.735
Vive la vie!

640
45:34.013 --> 45:36.489
- Vive la vie! - Vive la vie!

641
45:53.285 --> 45:54.622
Miss.

642
45:55.789 --> 45:57.037
Can I talk to you?

643
45:57.728 --> 45:59.299
There's something bothering me.

644
45:59.947 --> 46:02.509
About what you just said to Pro Vee...

645
46:03.225 --> 46:04.871
Don't you think she might feel

646
46:04.896 --> 46:07.460
like she's carrying the whole course on her shoulders?

647
46:08.015 --> 46:09.995
I just believe in Pro Vee.

648
46:10.020 --> 46:12.188
Believing in her is a good thing, Miss.

649
46:12.213 --> 46:14.895
But I wonder if all that expectation

650
46:14.920 --> 46:16.920
might feel like too much.

651
46:17.097 --> 46:20.512
Pro Vee really is a great pro, Miss.

652
46:20.537 --> 46:22.444
But if you take a step back,

653
46:22.469 --> 46:25.772
she's just a petite woman, just like you, Miss.

654
46:28.286 --> 46:29.692
You're right.

655
46:29.717 --> 46:32.384
I'll find a chance to talk to Pro Vee

656
46:32.409 --> 46:34.593
so she won't feel so stressed. How's that?

657
46:34.618 --> 46:35.715
Good.

658
46:36.247 --> 46:37.334
Vive la vie!

659
46:37.359 --> 46:38.525
Vive la vie!

660
46:51.682 --> 46:53.271
You didn't tag me by mistake, did you?

661
46:53.827 --> 46:54.962
I meant to invite you.

662
47:00.686 --> 47:01.726
Hungry?

663
47:02.732 --> 47:05.204
The competition's tomorrow. I need some encouragement.

664
47:05.229 --> 47:06.347
The usual?

665
47:07.074 --> 47:09.701
Uncle, two dry chicken noodles, please.

666
47:09.726 --> 47:11.100
And two bowls of broth, please.

667
47:11.125 --> 47:13.125
Oh, the usual. Coming right up.

668
47:13.426 --> 47:14.486
- Tomorrow... - Tomorrow...

669
47:16.179 --> 47:17.282
You go first.

670
47:17.831 --> 47:20.014
Give it your all tomorrow.

671
47:20.039 --> 47:21.191
That's all?

672
47:21.939 --> 47:25.907
Don't forget, tomorrow we'll still be on opposite sides.

673
47:25.932 --> 47:28.783
I believe both Goodview and The Royal Green

674
47:28.808 --> 47:30.141
will give it their all, too.

675
47:30.165 --> 47:32.829
And no matter how the competition turns out,

676
47:32.854 --> 47:34.854
no matter which side I have to stand on,

677
47:35.582 --> 47:38.615
my heart will always be on your side, Pro Jin.

678
47:44.248 --> 47:46.642
Here come the noodles!

679
47:46.667 --> 47:50.507
There you go. All set.

680
47:50.634 --> 47:52.314
No shumai pair today?

681
47:53.084 --> 47:55.807
I don't think you need to pair up anymore.

682
47:55.843 --> 47:59.813
Looks like you've already... paired up.

683
48:00.137 --> 48:04.284
There you go, that sweet smile. Make yourselves at home.

684
48:09.217 --> 48:11.320
No matter what happens tomorrow,

685
48:12.423 --> 48:15.129
- I want to tell you... - I don't want to hear it yet.

686
48:16.923 --> 48:19.017
Can I wait until after the competition?

687
48:21.950 --> 48:23.378
Let's eat.

688
48:23.454 --> 48:25.516
You should get to bed early tonight.

689
48:25.723 --> 48:27.931
So you're at your best tomorrow.

690
48:35.934 --> 48:38.435
Here. Eat plenty.

691
48:39.072 --> 48:40.331
That's enough, don't you think?

692
48:40.882 --> 48:42.850
You need your strength for tomorrow.

693
48:52.371 --> 48:53.768
Still tastes just as good.

694
48:54.141 --> 48:55.752
Just as good every time.

695
49:05.086 --> 49:06.195
Vee...

696
49:07.203 --> 49:09.846
About what I said at the meeting this afternoon...

697
49:10.063 --> 49:12.748
Did it make you feel pressured?

698
49:13.811 --> 49:15.121
What do you mean?

699
49:15.567 --> 49:17.274
When I made it sound like

700
49:17.299 --> 49:19.656
you had to carry everything on your own,

701
49:19.681 --> 49:23.081
the whole course and all my hopes.

702
49:24.217 --> 49:28.078
Mm. It was a little overwhelming,

703
49:28.103 --> 49:30.495
but I understand you, Nana.

704
49:30.535 --> 49:31.940
And more importantly,

705
49:31.964 --> 49:34.045
I'm not carrying anything on my shoulders.

706
49:34.671 --> 49:36.480
I'm choosing to do this,

707
49:36.505 --> 49:38.375
and I'll give it everything I've got.

708
49:38.446 --> 49:39.854
Not because anyone forced me to.

709
49:41.745 --> 49:44.459
And I believe you'll do it, Vee.

710
49:44.484 --> 49:46.607
I'll be cheering you on all the way.

711
49:48.234 --> 49:50.234
What if I lose?

712
49:50.262 --> 49:53.073
Then you lose. It's a competition.

713
49:53.255 --> 49:56.854
What's more important is that you get to be yourself again.

714
49:57.562 --> 49:59.160
Be myself again?

715
49:59.604 --> 50:02.146
To find happiness again in what you love.

716
50:02.297 --> 50:05.459
To be brave enough to compete, without being stuck in the past,

717
50:05.484 --> 50:07.484
and stop running from yourself.

718
50:10.130 --> 50:13.959
And if I had to choose between the course and your feelings,

719
50:14.514 --> 50:16.022
I'd choose you.

720
50:18.309 --> 50:19.393
Thank you.

721
50:39.299 --> 50:40.688
That's enough.

722
50:40.712 --> 50:43.338
You won't have any energy left tomorrow, then blame me.

723
51:02.803 --> 51:04.895
Hurry up and prove to me

724
51:04.920 --> 51:08.199
that our course will win before the 18th hole.

725
51:10.147 --> 51:13.023
And finally, representing our course,

726
51:13.048 --> 51:17.542
Pro Venus from Goodview Golf Club!

727
51:21.472 --> 51:24.351
When you love someone, you don't hold them back.

728
51:24.376 --> 51:26.705
You help push each other forward,

729
51:26.730 --> 51:28.523
so the person you love can reach their dreams,

730
51:28.548 --> 51:30.055
just like I did for you.

731
51:34.036 --> 51:38.452
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

732
51:38.837 --> 51:43.903
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

733
51:43.928 --> 51:49.306
♪ Together, we'll race toward the line ♪

734
51:49.331 --> 51:54.462
♪ Chasing the dream that's yours and mine ♪

735
51:54.487 --> 51:59.529
♪ In the end, I know we'll make it there ♪

736
51:59.554 --> 52:04.680
♪ Just one rule for you and me to share ♪

737
52:04.705 --> 52:07.787
♪ Promise you'll stay close to me ♪

738
52:07.812 --> 52:10.296
♪ Hold me in your arms so tenderly ♪

739
52:10.321 --> 52:15.905
♪ I've never bowed to anyone in sight ♪

740
52:15.930 --> 52:19.053
♪ But for you, I'd surrender without a fight ♪

741
52:19.078 --> 52:23.793
♪ Just take my hand and hold it tight ♪

742
52:25.076 --> 52:28.298
♪ And walk with me along the way ♪

743
52:28.323 --> 52:30.899
♪ No matter what it takes to win someday ♪

744
52:30.924 --> 52:36.515
♪ Sometimes this tender heart may despair ♪

745
52:36.540 --> 52:39.780
♪ But tell me, why should we care? ♪

746
52:39.805 --> 52:42.204
♪ When all we need is love that's fair ♪

747
52:42.229 --> 52:45.943
♪ In a love we share, no one has to win or lose ♪

748
52:47.900 --> 52:52.593
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

749
52:53.133 --> 52:58.282
♪ A thousand rounds, it'd still choose you ♪

750
52:58.307 --> 53:02.063
♪ One look in your eyes is all I need ♪
